  "analysis": "Both responses outline lanes, approval gates, CI constraints, and rollback plans, and address out‑of‑order buffering and irreversible schema changes. BGX more directly mirrors the repository facts—explicitly excludes the flaky network check from required CI passes, ties unit‑test‑only PR runs to credit limits, includes a dedicated legacy‑polling cleanup lane, and spells out a canary rollout with feature‑flag control—reducing likely follow‑up questions. FMX is thorough but slightly more abstract and omits some of those concrete CI and cleanup details.",
